{"title":"1985 IMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems of the 26th IMO Finland.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_I\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day I</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_II\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day II</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_I\">Day I</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day I\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A circle has center on the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of the cyclic quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.  The other three sides are tangent to the circle.  Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5e35daf09d12b065ceddb37704dc5aef9d3f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD + BC = AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"132\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be given relatively prime natural numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/6/7b69542b4470fc340f255ae145f3fb07ab2352dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />.  Each number in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4124604e7d932632d9158fac06cae0b86cd0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M = \\{ 1,2, \\ldots , n-1 \\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"18\" /> is colored either blue or white.  It is given that\n</p><p>(i) for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/3/0b3761ddd238750d004e59905c71dbebed4f8df7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" />, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca318ea13591cc525ed0841ab6c0fff917a6633c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-i$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" /> have the same color;\n</p><p>(ii) for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82fa891ad392f6d2ee0c9b319c053b25a51ea562.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in M, i \\neq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59db9bc0f05acaccf44eef992a638f9e7bbf29e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|i-k|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" /> have the same color.\n</p><p>Prove that all the numbers in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> have the same color.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For any polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/e/1fe5d52410379411b2041f59ded55b98e7dedd94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = a_0 + a_1 x + \\cdots + a_k x^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"230\" height=\"20\" /> with integer coefficients, the number of coefficients which are odd is denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/d/95d33b7b4feb5e94e1ceaab9070342d9d25d3d0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w(P)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" />.  For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d421cc13e7243f73abcc08af3efb0dd38aeaf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 0, 1, \\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45380490a52bb5384d110d7b680d337d02de8425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_i (x) = (1+x)^i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"19\" />.  Prove that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f5776f619f1709dddd0946754b3015d2599eeeb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i_1, i_2, \\ldots , i_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> are integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f149a3fa5a6e977ca36f925df7d3b8d8a358df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\leq i_1 &lt; i_2 &lt; \\cdots &lt; i_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"169\" height=\"15\" />, then\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edc5dc71da096f9e7bba32042a1e1e683157f148.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w(Q_{i_1} + Q_{i_2} + \\cdots + Q_{i_n}) \\ge w(Q_{i_1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"273\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_II\">Day II</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day II\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Given a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e84b93cdfb6fff7a9d090e34212e05e8bfe42b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1985$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> distinct positive integers, none of which has a prime divisor greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> contains a subset of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> elements whose product is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th power of an integer.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> passes through the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and intersects the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> again at distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the point of intersection of the circumcircles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1590a6dd5bd44d78ef74b499874afebfd3ac4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KBN$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> (apart from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />). Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/9063f273653119f7fd7d25519993eb166e4f94b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OMB = 90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"110\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For every real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, construct the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/679d0a6d6cef45b71d1a66078ca115bdca133558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,x_2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"11\" /> by setting:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b07253b1bc28335448ea066d4dde47845f39c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n + 1} = x_n(x_n + {1\\over n}).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"154\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Prove that there exists exactly one value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/e/e7ec9115d800c1a51b52b9dd126a761c3946afa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; x_n &lt; x_{n + 1} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO\" title=\"1985 IMO\">1985 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=1&amp;cid=16&amp;year=1985\">IMO 1985 problems on the Resources page</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\">IMO Problems and Solutions, with authors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO\" title=\"1985 IMO\">1985 IMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_IMO\" title=\"1984 IMO\">1984 IMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1985 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_IMO\" title=\"1986 IMO\">1986 IMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018021722\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 284/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 837/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8162/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.645      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.645      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4141:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018021722 and revision id 150537. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}